{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SeminormalWeight"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.reducedWeight_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.reducedWeight_pair","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L67-L78","doc":"**Box-pair pairing** — the cell-geometry form of `g_ρ + g_{−ρ} = 1`. For two\noff-diagonal cells (`q^{2·ρ(a,b)} ≠ 1`, i.e. `a`, `b` not on the same\ndiagonal in the sense that makes the weight degenerate), the reduced\nseminormal weights at the two orientations of the pair sum to `1`. Composing\nInfra 1 (`axialDistance_antisymm`) with Infra 2 (`reducedWeight_add_neg`):\neach off-diagonal box pair contributes exactly `1` to the reduced-weight sum,\nwhich is *why* `χ_λ(σ)/h = c_λ ∈ ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance_self","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Axial distance is antisymmetric**: `ρ(a,b) = −ρ(b,a)`. This is the\ncell-geometry root of the seminormal ρ ↔ −ρ pairing — swapping the two boxes\n(the `i ↔ i+1` transposition acting on a standard tableau) negates `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_diag","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L53-L55","doc":"Cells on the same diagonal (shifted by `(k,k)`) share a content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_col_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_col_step","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L50-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_row_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content_row_step","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L47-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.axialDistance","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L42-L45","doc":"**Axial distance** between two cells: the difference of their contents. For the\nboxes holding `i` and `i+1` in a standard tableau this is the `ρ` of the\nseminormal weight `a_ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauContent.content","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauContent.lean#L28-L40","doc":"**Content of a cell** `(i, j)`: column index minus row index, `c(i,j) = j − i`.\nCells on the same diagonal share a content; it is the seminormal-form\ncoordinate of a box.\n\nOverlap note (reuse audit): `QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.content (i j : ℕ)` carries\nthe same `j − i` formula in two-argument shape. This file keeps the *pair*-shaped\nversion deliberately — it is a lightweight foundational brick (imports only\n`Mathlib.Tactic` + the weight layer), whereas `Hoefsmit` sits on the heavy\n`Wedderburn`/`Matrix.Charpoly` cone. The correct consolidation direction is to\nextract this pair primitive here and have `Hoefsmit` depend on it, not to pull\nthe heavy cone into the combinatorial base; tracked as a follow-up, not done in\nthis PR to avoid coupling the brick to `Hoefsmit`'s dependencies. ","signatureChunk":0}]}